ENGLISH
────────────────────────────────────────

1. Free use
   You may download Frieze Bender from its official sources
   (github.com/montechnicien218/courbeur-de-frise and montechnicien.ch) and use it
   free of charge, for private or professional purposes.
   What you make with the tool (DXF or SVG files, engraved or cut objects) belongs to you:
   you may use and sell it freely.

2. Not allowed without the author's prior written permission
   a) modifying, adapting or translating the software, or creating derivative works;
   b) copying or redistributing the software, in whole or in part (source code, page,
      program, example files), other than from its official sources;
   c) selling, renting or sublicensing the software, or including it in another product
      or service;
   d) removing or changing copyright and licence notices.
   Sharing a link to the official sources is always allowed.

3. Visible source code
   The source code is published for transparency, so anyone can check what the program
   does. Reading it, and building it without any change for your own use, is allowed.
   This grants no other right.

4. Example files (examples/ folder)
   You may use them for your own work, including work you sell. Reselling or
   redistributing the files themselves is not allowed.

5. Third-party components
   Third-party components (Clipper, opentype.js, fonts) remain under their own licences,
   described in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.

6. Earlier versions
   Versions 1.12.0, 1.12.1 and 1.13.0 were released under the MIT licence; copies of those
   versions obtained at the time remain under that licence. This licence applies from
   version 1.13.1 on.

7. No warranty
   The software is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind. To the fullest extent
   permitted by law, the author is not liable for any damage arising from its use,
   including on a laser machine.

8. Governing law
   This licence is governed by Swiss law. Place of jurisdiction: Biel/Bienne (canton of Bern).

Permissions and questions: info@montechnicien.ch
